<Layout title="ETF News Daily Privacy Policy and Cookie Information" description="Read how ETF News Daily handles calculator inputs, optional analytics, consent defaults and cookies, with advertising disabled until separate compliance review."><article class="paper"><h1>ETF News Daily Privacy Policy and Cookie Information</h1><p class="lead">This static site does not need an account or personal portfolio data.</p><p>Updated October 16, 2026</p><p>Calculator inputs stay in your browser and are not submitted to an application server.</p><p>Hosting providers may process connection logs.</p><p>Analytics and advertising account configuration does not mean tracking is active: GA4 loads only when a valid public measurement ID is configured. Advertising remains disabled.</p><p>When enabled, GA4 processes page views and calculator-use events, not input amounts. Consent Mode defaults deny analytics and advertising storage and advertising user data/personalization in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, and grant them elsewhere. Denied consent can still send cookieless measurement pings. These defaults are not a consent banner or a certified consent-management platform; none is currently integrated.</p><p>A Google-certified consent platform must be integrated before ad requests for EEA, UK and Switzerland visitors.</p><p>Browser controls can block or delete cookies; Google advertising preferences are available at myadcenter.google.com.</p><p>Contact the site for privacy questions.</p><h2>Keep reading</h2><p><a href="/tools/">Explore the cost models</a> · <a href="/filings/">Inspect SEC filings</a></p><p>Official reference: <a href="https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/exchange-traded-funds-etfs">SEC Investor.gov: exchange-traded funds</a></p></article></Layout>